 "title": "DeepSeek updates its Flash API model to V4.1-Flash-1017",
 "summary": "DeepSeek documents V4.1-Flash-1017 as the current target behind `deepseek-flash`; the API calling method and pricing remain unchanged.",
 "research_notes": "For the hosted model, keep the existing API integration and set the model to `deepseek-flash`; it resolves to the current V4.1 Flash release.\n\nFor local experimentation, install updated Transformers and Accelerate, then load `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017` through the documented image-text-to-text pipeline or `AutoModelForCausalLM` path.\n\nUse the stable `deepseek-flash` API name instead of embedding the checkpoint name in hosted integrations, so the documented current version is selected without changing the call format.\n\nWhen self-hosting, start from an officially documented Transformers or vLLM loading path rather than assuming an older V4 Flash runtime configuration works unchanged.",
